# Run OUTPUT is ignored; an experiment's SOURCE is not. Without these
# exceptions every new runs/<experiment>/ had to be `git add -f`-ed by hand,
# and one forgotten add means the Colab notebook clones a repo with no script
# in it. Only the top level of each experiment dir is exempt, so the data
# underneath (results/, raw/, rollouts.npz, figures) stays out of the repo.
runs/*
!runs/*/
runs/*/*
!runs/*/README.md
!runs/*/*.py
!runs/*/*.yaml
!runs/*/*.csv
.archive/
benchmarks/
.sources/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.bal


# Ignore all dotted folders
.*/
